<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amira Dubbaj</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1536</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Muzaffar Sultan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amira Dubbaj, also called Muzaffar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>, was the Ishaqid ruler of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a>, on the Caspian coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the early 16th century. He married a daughter of the Safavid shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a>, linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>-rich province to the new dynasty. He later rebelled against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahmasp-i">Shah Tahmasp I</a>, was captured and was executed in the 1530s.</p></div>
